 "purpose": "The curriculum as a menu: Subject > Domain > Topic, with the practice forms (modes) per topic. All menus, cheat sheets and the report grouping come from here.",
 "details": "No other menu file contains the names of subjects, domains or topics. Ids are menu ids (fixed); `opslag` points to the stored skill ids (kern skills and snelrekenen.<kind>) that never change. A mode or a cheat sheet is a function f(app, breadcrumb) that starts an existing screen. The dataclasses Spiekbrief, Onderwerp, Domein and Vak describe the tree; VAKKEN (Wiskunde, Taal) is imported lazily from wiskunde.py and taal.py at the bottom of the module. Helper functions search the tree and produce the data the core needs (the report grouping `indeling` and the themes of mixed practice `gemengd_themas`). BINNENKORT (subjects shown grey in the main menu) is currently always empty because Taal is a real subject now.",
 "module_docstring": "Het leerplan als menu: Vak → Domein → Onderwerp, met per onderwerp de oefenvormen (modi).",
